   (lut:bind-command "WINDOW and COMMAND must be live. WIDGET optionally identifies a button/menu button; a control may have one active binding. CONTEXT defaults to WINDOW; CONTEXT-FUNCTION optionally takes WINDOW to obtain dynamic data. SHORTCUT-P defaults T. Binding owns label/enabled state until unbound. Detached controls are inactive until adopted by WINDOW. Existing activation handlers are retained." "COMMAND-BINDING. On registration errors, connections and references are rolled back." "(let* ((w (lut:make-widget 'lut:window)) (b (lut:add-child w (lut:make-widget 'lut:button))) (c (lut:make-command :hello \"Hello\" (lambda (c context) (declare (ignore c context)))))) (lut:bind-command w c :widget b))")
